estment advisory and structured finance services. The company operates through three segments: Asset Management, Medical Device, and Corporate and Other. The Asset Management segment provides investment advisory services and acts as sub-advisor to a series of exchange-traded funds, with products offered through exchange-traded funds and separate accounts. The Medical Device segment sells medical devices, generating revenue from software licensing, fee-per-test arrangements, and hardware sales. The Corporate and Other segment maintains a Bitcoin treasury strategy, acquiring and holding Bitcoin as a primary reserve asset, and issues preferred equity securities, including SATA and SATS. The company also operates an at-the-market equity program for continuous issuance of Class A common stock and SATA preferred stock. Strive, Inc. was formerly known as Asset Entities Inc. and changed its name to Strive, Inc. in September 2025. Strive, Inc. was incorporated in 2022 and is based in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew Ryan Cole C.F.A. | Chairman & CEO | Age 40 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 28 people. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Strive, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.8B market cap.","The top line has compounded at +36% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -265% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advan